  "boundReadingFields": [
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "Λέγω δή, ὅτι παρὰ τὰ εἰρημένα πέντε σχήματα οὐ συσταθήσεται ἕτερον σχῆμα περιεχόμενον ὑπὸ ἰσοπλεύρων τε καὶ ἰσογωνίων ἴσων ἀλλήλοις.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 4,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "Iam dico, praeter quinque figuras, quas nominauimus, nullam aliam construi posse polygonis et aequilateris et aequiangulis inter se aequalibus comprehensam.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 4,
          "mcid": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "I now say that, besides the five figures already mentioned, no other figure will be constructed that is enclosed by equilateral and equiangular figures equal to one another.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 4,
          "mcid": 2
        },
        {
          "page": 4,
          "mcid": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "Ὑπὸ μὲν γὰρ δύο τριγώνων ἢ ὅλως ἐπιπέδων στερεὰ γωνία οὐ συνίσταται.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 5,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "Nam ex duobus triangulis aut omnino figuris planis angulus solidus construi nequit.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 5,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "For a solid angle is not formed by two triangles, or by two plane figures in general.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 5,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 5,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "ὑπὸ δὲ τριῶν τριγώνων ἡ τῆς πυραμίδος, ὑπὸ δὲ τεσσάρων ἡ τοῦ ὀκταέδρου, ὑπὸ δὲ πέντε ἡ τοῦ εἰκοσαέδρου·",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "ex tribus uero triangulis angulus pyramidis construitur, ex quattuor octaedri, ex quinque icosaedri.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "From three triangles comes the corner of the pyramid; from four, that of the octahedron; from five, that of the icosahedron.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 6,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "οὔσης γὰρ τῆς τοῦ ἰσοπλεύρου τριγώνου γωνίας διμοίρου ὀρθῆς ἔσονται αἱ ἓξ τέσσαρσιν ὀρθαῖς ἴσαι· ὅπερ ἀδύνατον·",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 7,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "nam cum angulus trianguli aequilateri duae partes sint recti, sex anguli quattuor rectis aequales erunt; quod fieri non potest;",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 7,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "For, since the angle of an equilateral triangle is two thirds of a right angle, the six angles will equal four right angles—which is impossible here.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 7,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 7,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "ἅπασα γὰρ στερεὰ γωνία ὑπὸ ἐλασσόνων ἢ τεσσάρων ὀρθῶν περιέχεται.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 8,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "nam omnis angulus solidus minus quattuor rectis comprehenditur.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 8,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "For every solid angle is enclosed by face angles whose sum is less than four right angles.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 8,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 8,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "ὑπὸ δὲ τετραγώνων τριῶν ἡ τοῦ κύβου γωνία περιέχεται· ὑπὸ δὲ τεσσάρων ἀδύνατον· ἔσονται γὰρ πάλιν τέσσαρες ὀρθαί.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 9,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "tribus autem quadratis angulus cubi comprehenditur. quattuor autem nullus; nam rursus quattuor recti erunt.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 9,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "The corner of the cube is enclosed by three squares. Four cannot enclose such a corner: once again there would be four right angles.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 9,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 9,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "οὔσης γὰρ τῆς τοῦ πενταγώνου ἰσοπλεύρου γωνίας ὀρθῆς καὶ πέμπτου, ἔσονται αἱ τέσσαρες γωνίαι τεσσάρων ὀρθῶν μείζους· ὅπερ ἀδύνατον.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "nam cum angulus pentagoni aequilateri aequalis sit recto angulo cum quinta parte recti, quattuor anguli quattuor rectis maiores erunt; quod fieri non potest.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "For, since the angle of the equilateral pentagon is a right angle and a fifth of a right angle, four such angles will exceed four right angles—which is impossible here.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 10,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 10,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "Ἄλλως· στερεὰ γωνία ἐστὶν ἡ ὑπὸ πλειόνων ἢ δύο γωνιῶν ἐπιπέδων περιεχομένη μὴ οὐσῶν ἐν τῷ αὐτῷ ἐπιπέδῳ πρὸς ἑνὶ σημείῳ συνισταμένων.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 11,
          "mcid": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "Aliter. Solidus angulus est, qui amplius quam duobus angulis planis continetur non in eodem plano positis et ad unum punctum coniunctis.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 11,
          "mcid": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "Alternatively: a solid angle is enclosed by more than two plane angles, not lying in the same plane, coming together at one point.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 11,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 11,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "grc",
      "text": "Ὅτι δὲ ἡ τοῦ ἰσοπλεύρου καὶ ἰσογωνίου πενταγώνου γωνία ὀρθή ἐστι καὶ πέμπτου, οὕτω δεικτέον.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 12,
          "mcid": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "la",
      "text": "Angulum autem pentagoni aequilateri et aequianguli aequalem esse angulo recto et quintae parti recti, sic demonstrandum.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 12,
          "mcid": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "text": "That the angle of an equilateral and equiangular pentagon is a right angle and a fifth must be shown as follows.",
      "pageContent": [
        {
          "page": 12,
          "mcid": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 12,
          "mcid": 9
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
